.TH FL-AUTOROTATE 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.4" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-autorotate \- turn the built-in screen with the device
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-autorotate\fR [\fB\-\-set\fR normal|left-up|right-up|bottom-up]
.SH DESCRIPTION
On convertibles and tablets, follows the accelerometer of
\fBiio-sensor-proxy\fR and turns the built-in screen (eDP, LVDS or DSI) with
the device, through wlr-output-management. It starts with the session and
quits at once on computers without a rotation sensor. Settings > Displays >
"Turn the built-in screen with the device" switches it off
(\fB[Display] AutoRotate=false\fR in \fIdesktop.ini\fR). \fB\-\-set\fR turns the
screen once and exits.
.PP
In tablet mode (a convertible folded back) \fBfl-wm\fR(1) brings up the
on-screen keyboard when a text field has the focus.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
\fBFLD_ROTATE_OUTPUT\fR names the output to turn instead of the built-in one.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-osk\fR(1)
